variant esp32tht of ../esp32/hardware/graph.circuit
  set name "christmas-bell-esp32tht"
  set version "0.1"
  set date "2026-10-31"
  description "Automatic Christmas bell, variant ESP32 THT (D-23): the circuit of the variant ESP32 – a LILYGO
      T-Display V1.1 (ESP32, 1.14 inch TFT) instead of the Nano, 3.3 V logic, yellow-green LEDs (D-13, D-14) – with
      through-hole parts only and no assembly, like the variant THT (D-12): a bare board to solder by hand."
  purpose private market EU
    notes "Automatic Christmas bell, ESP32 THT variant, for the owner's home, built and used by the owner – not sold
        or given away (D-16). Powered through the T-Display's USB-C only – no cell at the module's battery input, no
        mains. The T-Display's ESP32 uses Wi-Fi (2.4 GHz, channels 1-13): a web page in the owner's home network –
        status and control of the countdown, no internet service – and a setup hotspot (WPA2) until the home network
        is set (D-17); Bluetooth stays off."

  part U1
    notes "Plugs into two 1x12 female headers KH-2.54FH-1X12P-H8.5 (C2905419), pitch 2.54 mm, rows 22.86 mm apart
      (hand-soldered, [[extra]] in edakit.toml). Powered through its USB-C socket; its 5V pin (VBUS behind the
      module's 1N5819) supplies the servo and C1, its 3V3 pin (AP2112K) the buttons. Strapping pins IO12/IO15/IO2 and
      the second 3V3 pin stay free. LCSC C18722937 is a stand-in for the EasyEDA device: its symbol and footprint are
      rebuilt in the project (D-13)."
  part J1 connector PZ254V-11-03P lcsc C2937625 no-bom "Servo (GND, +5 V, signal)"
    notes "Standard servo plug: brown = GND (1), red = +5 V (2), orange = signal (3). THT header as on the variant THT
      (D-12)."
  part C1 capacitor "1000uF 16V" lcsc C439782 no-bom "Buffer capacitor for the servo"
    notes "Absorbs the servo's start-up peaks so the ESP32 does not reset. THT radial Ø10 × 13 mm as on the variant
      THT (D-12)."
  part LED5 led XL-504SYGD lcsc C2895551 no-bom "5 mm LED, yellow-green, countdown step 1"
  part LED4 led XL-504SYGD lcsc C2895551 no-bom "5 mm LED, yellow-green, countdown step 2"
  part LED3 led XL-504UYD lcsc C2895495 no-bom "5 mm LED, yellow, countdown step 3"
  part LED2 led XL-504UYD lcsc C2895495 no-bom "5 mm LED, yellow, countdown step 4"
  part LED1 led XL-504SURD lcsc C2895493 no-bom "5 mm LED, red, countdown step 5"
    notes "As on the variant THT: the footprint marks pad 1 as anode (+) – symbol name K, role anode (parts entry)"
  for n in 4..5
    part LED{n}
      notes "D-23: yellow-green as on the variant ESP32 (D-14) – the 3.3 V outputs do not drive a 3 V green evenly;
        XL-504SYGD, VF 2.0–2.6 V at 20 mA"
  for n in 2..3
    part LED{n}
      notes "As on the variant THT: pin 2 = anode, the footprint's \"+\" at pad 2"
  for n in 1..5
    part LED{n}
      accept LIM.p -
  for n in 3..4
    part R{n} resistor "100 Ω 1/4 W metal film, THT" lcsc C57438 value 100Ω no-bom
      notes "D-23: 100 Ω as on the variant ESP32 (D-14) – the yellow-green XL-504SYGD at full current"
  part R1 resistor "330 Ω 1/4 W metal film, THT" lcsc C58608 value 330Ω no-bom
  part R2 resistor "330 Ω 1/4 W metal film, THT" lcsc C58608 value 330Ω no-bom
  part R5 resistor "330 Ω 1/4 W metal film, THT" lcsc C58608 value 330Ω no-bom
  for n in 1..2
    part R{n}
      notes "D-23: 330 Ω – red and yellow dimmed towards the yellow-green's brightness (owner's decision):
        XL-504SURD/UYD give 400–900 mcd at 20 mA, the XL-504SYGD 50–200 mcd"
  part R5
    notes "D-23: 330 Ω – red and yellow dimmed towards the yellow-green's brightness (owner's decision):
      XL-504SURD/UYD give 400–900 mcd at 20 mA, the XL-504SYGD 50–200 mcd"
  for n in 6..7
    part R{n} resistor "4.7 kΩ 1/4 W metal film, THT" lcsc C57204 value 4.7kΩ no-bom
  for n in 8..9
    part R{n} resistor "100 Ω 1 W metal film, THT" lcsc C119469 value 100Ω no-bom
      notes "Keeps a power bank from switching off (D-8): the module alone draws at least 0.04 A (i_core_min_a), with
        the base load R8 ∥ R9 the board at least about 0.14 A (simulated)."
  for n in 1..2
    part S{n} button K2-1102DP-C4SW-04 lcsc C110153 no-bom

  layout fixed U1 LED1 LED2 LED3 LED4 LED5 S1 S2 J1
  layout edge U1
  layout note "LED5, LED4, LED3, LED2, LED1 form the countdown row, in this order from left to right, as on every
      board; their anodes on one side (the footprints differ: LED1's \"+\" at pad 1, LED2-LED5's anode at pad 2)."
  layout note "U1 plugs into two 1x12 female headers 22.86 mm apart, display up, USB-C at the board edge; mark its 5V
      pin (U1.1) on the silkscreen – the pin field is symmetric."
  layout note "R8 and R9 dissipate 0.25 W each: apart from each other and from C1; the builder lets them stand 1-2 mm
      above the board."
  layout note "LED4 and LED5 (footprint LED-TH_BD5.9-P2.54-RD_GREEN) show only the flat at the cathode, no \"+\" and
      no square pad."
  layout near C1 J1

  accept HINT.debounce "debounced in the ESP32 firmware variants/esp32/firmware like buttons.ino (50 ms, D-17) – the
      same firmware runs on this board"
